## 22. FIRESTORE SECURITY

If Firebase Firestore is used, create security rules based on authenticated identity and resource ownership.

Rules must ensure:
- Users can update only permitted fields of their own profiles.
- Private user information is not publicly readable.
- Only authorized participants can access an exchange.
- Only permitted participants can update an exchange.
- Messages are accessible only to conversation participants.
- Notifications cannot be forged or read by unauthorized users.
- Achievements cannot be self-awarded through unrestricted client writes.
- Administrative privileges cannot be granted by ordinary users.

Validate important business rules on a trusted backend when necessary.

Do not use unrestricted production rules such as allowing every user to read and write every document.

Include instructions for configuring and testing security rules.

